    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0041" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 401.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatches, from No. 451 to No. 454,
                    both inclusive, are duly received. No. 451 requests me to use my best endeavors
                    to procure evidence of the connexion of Bravay &amp; Co. with the insurgents.
                    Mr. Dudley, United States consul at Liverpool, had already informed me of the
                    want of this evidence, and I had made such inquiries as were in my power; and,
                    furthermore, had consulted with the English embassy here on this subject. I have
                    no doubt that such connexion between Bravay and the insurgents exists, but I
                    know not if evidence can be found to prove it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
